{"ts":"2026-05-29T15:44:53.057Z","author":"codex","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-web-onv4"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Server hangs/cryptic error when DATABASE_URL is unset"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"SYMPTOM: Starting pm-web without DATABASE_URL produced no output for several seconds, then a cryptic 'getaddrinfo EAI_AGAIN pm-telemetry-postgres' DNS error. db.ts silently fell back to a hardcoded telemetry-specific host (pm-telemetry-postgres) with undefined credentials, and the failure only surfaced after the 5s pool connectionTimeout. REPRO: env -u DATABASE_URL node dist/server.js  (observed ~5s silent wait then DNS error stack). EXPECTED: a server that requires a DB should fail fast with a clear actionable message and exit non-zero. OBSERVED vs EXPECTED: cryptic delayed DNS error vs clear 'DATABASE_URL is not set' guidance. FIX: added assertDbConfigured() in db.ts (validates DATABASE_URL or POSTGRES_HOST+POSTGRES_DB, removed the pm-telemetry-postgres default), called at the top of server.ts before any DB use; also collapsed the schema-init catch to print err.message instead of a full stack. Now: no DATABASE_URL -> instant clear message + exit 1 (1s); unreachable DB -> clean one-line timeout error + exit 1."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":[]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-05-29T15:44:53.057Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-05-29T15:44:53.057Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-web-ul0n"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"3d55f135a8d4363798e4bf1e1ecb8d53a11496408b8282f883947fc5924ad389","message":""}
